  "messages": "ellie (design): quick sync \u2014 accessibility + UX tweaks for playground streaming UI. prototyping a few states: aria for live stream, stop/regenerate placement, token counter visibility, prompt lib keyboard nav. want quick calls before dev passes.\nellie (design): attaching notes \u2014 thinking about aria-live behavior and keyboard-first controls. open to alternate copy for token counter (used vs remaining).\nkevin (eng): nice \u2014 big dev constraints: streaming updates come as partial tokens, updating DOM per chunk. aria-live can be noisy if set to 'assertive' for every chunk.\nanya (ux): agree with kevin. suggestion: use aria-live=\"polite\" for the transcript region and a visually-hidden status region that updates with concise messages (e.g., \"response streaming: 4s\") for screen readers.\ntom (frontend): example we prototyped:\n```html\n<div id=\"chat-stream\" role=\"log\" aria-live=\"polite\" aria-atomic=\"false\">...chunks...</div>\n<span id=\"stream-status\" class=\"sr-only\" aria-live=\"assertive\">Streaming started</span>\n```\nkevin (eng): that looks good. one small note: keep DOM patches cheap \u2014 append text node + update status once every 300ms to avoid layout thrash.\nmaria (pm): copy question \u2014 users confused by token counter phrasing in tests. Should we show \"Tokens used: 123/4000\" or \"Tokens left: 3,877\"? also color/contrast for small counter.\nanya (ux): lean toward \"Tokens left\" as primary, show used on hover. color: use high-contrast text + chip with 3.5:1 min and add an icon-only verbose tooltip for colorblind. also keyboard focusable.\nellie (design): accessibility nits: visible focus ring on the counter, and when tokens are low show a non-intrusive banner with action to shorten prompt.\ntom (frontend): technical \u2014 we can render counter as <button> so it's keyboard focusable and opens the token helper panel. works with existing code.\nkevin (eng): agreed. implement helper panel off-canvas; ok to wire button semantics.\nellie (design): stop/regenerate button placement debate: current mock puts both inside the message bubble toolbar. some say it should sit next to the prompt input so regens are clearly tied to the prompt. thoughts?\nmaria (pm): product intent: regenerate ties to the last assistant response, stop ties to in-flight response. keeping them visually together makes sense but needs clear affordance.\nanya (ux): proposed compromise: show primary action (Stop) inline on the streaming message while a secondary sticky control next to the prompt shows 'Regenerate' (and keyboard shortcut). when no streaming, hide Stop and elevate Regenerate beside input.\ntom (frontend): sticky control is doable; need to coordinate z-index with prompt library panel.\nkevin (eng): shortcut suggestions: Esc to stop stream, Cmd/Ctrl+R is taken by browser; suggest Alt+R or Ctrl+Shift+Enter for regenerate. also expose accessiblity labels like aria-label=\"Stop streaming\" and aria-disabled state.\nellie (design): microcopy options for buttons: Stop \u2014 \"Stop\" (clear), Regen \u2014 \"Regenerate response\" (verbose) or \"Retry\" (short). prefer \"Regenerate response\" for clarity.\nmaria (pm): prefer clarity \u2014 \"Regenerate response\". analytics team can aggregate events.\ndesign-bot: UX checklist added to #ux-board: focus states, aria-live policy, token counter copy, stop/regenerate shortcuts, prompt lib keyboard nav.\nellie (design): prompt library notes: keyboard-first nav, categories (Templates / Persona / Examples), drag reorder for favorites, quick-insert via Enter, and search-as-you-type with inline keyboard hints. also ensure items have role=\"option\" and list with role=\"listbox\" for screen readers.\nanya (ux): also add semantic announcements when an item is inserted: \"Inserted prompt: {title}\" in sr-only region.\ntom (frontend): implementation plan: we can reuse existing combobox component and extend with listbox ARIA roles. need design tokens for hover/focus.\nkevin (eng): dev estimate ~3w for full accessibility pass + keyboard shortcuts + token helper. can split into two sprints: streaming + stop + status; then prompt lib + tokens.\nellie (design): action items: 1) adopt aria-live=\"polite\" + super small sr-only assertive status for start/stop; 2) token counter primary label = \"Tokens left\" with accessible button to open helper; 3) stop inline, regenerate sticky next to input + keyboard shortcut (Ctrl+Shift+Enter), avoid browser collisions; 4) prompt library keyboard-first with listbox roles and sr-only insertion announcements. please thumbs-up or flag anything blocking.\nmaria (pm): thumbs-up from me. will add to next sprint planning doc.\nanya (ux): +1, I'll update the mock and include color-contrast specs.\ntom (frontend): +1 \u2014 I'll prototype the button-as-counter pattern.\nkevin (eng): +1, will break tickets.\nellie (design): thanks all \u2014 will drop updated comps and copy in the design thread later today :handshake:",
